    "section": "9.70",
    "heading": "Combat Encounters",
    "lineStart": 14370,
    "lineEnd": 14380
  },
  "section": "9.70",
  "rulesText": "The following features can make a combat encounter more interesting or challenging:\n\nChanges in Elevation. Terrain features that provide a change of elevation (such as stacks of empty crates, ledges, and balconies) reward clever positioning and encourage characters to jump, climb, fly, or teleport.\n\nDefensive Positions. Enemies in hard-to-reach locations or defensive positions force characters who normally attack at range to move around.\n\nMixed Monster Groups. When different types of monsters work together, they can combine their abilities - just like characters with different classes and origins. A diverse force is more powerful.\n\nReasons to Move. Use features that encourage characters and their enemies to move around, such as chandeliers, kegs of gunpowder or oil, and rolling stone traps."
}
